hrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.1634297912240277,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00782,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":5.2,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Beta Bionics, Inc., a commercial-stage medical device company, engages in the design, development, and commercialization of solutions to enhance the health and quality of life of insulin-requiring people with diabetes. It offers iLet Bionic Pancreas, an insulin delivery device for the treatment of type 1 diabetes in adults and children six years of age and older. The company is also developing Patch Pump, an insulin pump that is designed to adhere directly to the skin and administer insulin without the need for tubing; Bihormonal iLet, which combines automated delivery of insulin and glucagon; and iLet to treat people with insulin-dependent type-2 diabetes. It has collaboration and license agreement with Xeris Pharmaceuticals, Inc. (Xeris) to develop and commercialize a pump-compatible glucagon formulation; and development and commercialization agreement with Abbott Diabetes Care Inc. to develop and commercialize an automated insulin delivery system. The company was incorporated in 2015 and is headquartered in Irvine, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Sean T. Saint PE | President, CEO & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 420 people. Revenue per employee of $239K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $39K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Beta Bionics, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $854M market cap on $100M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +54% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -105% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 55% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $56M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Net dilution runs at 22.8% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 16% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 72% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $2.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 144% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"BBNX Deadline: BBNX Investors Have Opportunity to Lead Beta Bionics, Inc. Securities Fraud Lawsuit","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/bbnx-deadline-bbnx-investors-have-opportunity-to-lead-beta-bionics-inc-securities-fraud-lawsuit-302928332.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793744400.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.178,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"BBNX Deadline Today: Rosen Law Firm Urges Beta Bionics, Inc. (NASDAQ: BBNX) Stockholders to Contact the Firm for Information About Their Rights","source":"businesswire.com","link":"http://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20261103110064/en/BBNX-Deadline-Today-Rosen-Law-Firm-Urges-Beta-Bionics-Inc.-NASDAQ-BBNX-Stockholders-to-Contact-the-Firm-for-Information-About-Their-Rights/?feedref=JjAwJuNHiystnCoBq_hl-adS5VAKkf1zsgyV8tTPInVcgiwDl5F89IquLVWUqfRVgLxDkSKfgoruKb9yWl5as-PbWreMWuYBefATrZ0EPTVXw2Oldt-3VQjUwU4Zj5HZBSvR87oUDgbHejiywQBpbg%3D%3D","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793736180.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"ti